1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The Ray of Creation — Gurdjieff’s cosmology, as recorded by P. D. Ouspensky.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The Absolute: an emblem of unity, not a pictured celestial body.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:27,000
From innumerable worlds, we follow just one selected line.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Within that vast order, one starry world: our galaxy.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Our star belongs to this hierarchy; it does not stand alone.

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The next order contains the planets of our Sun.

7
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Each lower world is subject to more orders of laws.

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:26,000
A living Earth, further from the single will of the Absolute.

9
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Life receives planetary influences and mediates them toward Earth.

10
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:46,000
In this teaching, the growing end of the selected ray.

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:55,000
More orders of law mean less freedom from mechanical influence.

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The moving constraints are a metaphor — not literal physical laws.
